dcc80-6b974 | 2026-07-04T13:49:14Z | session:dcc80382-bcc0-45ea-8b9c-1a2fc741f872 | <teammate-message teammate_id="feed-empty-diagnosis" color="red" summary="No schema mismatch — it&apos;s projection_rev (NMP #2952). Chirp guards PR #44."> \n Both done — but with an important correction: there is NO schema/key mismatch. I inspected both host decoders at chirp master (post #38/#41) and they already match the emitted descriptor exactly. \n  \n ## (b) Result: NOT a schema/key mismatch — it's the projection_rev contract \n - Android `TypedHomeFeedDecoder.kt`: `PROJECTION_KEY="chirp.timeline.home"`, `SCHEMA_ID="nmp.note_feed.opfeed"`, `FILE_IDENTIFIER="NNFS"`; it even documents the retired `NOFS`/`nmp.nip01.opfeed` v1 as gone (chirp#35 done). \n - iOS `TypedHomeFeedDecoder.swift`: identical — `projectionKey="chirp.timeline.home"`, `schemaId="nmp.note_feed.opfeed"`, `fileIdentifier="NNFS"`. \n Both gate on `key == PROJECTION_KEY && schemaId == SCHEMA_ID` with the correct values. chirp#35's migration is correct; nothing to fix there. \n  \n The golden-pass/live-fail signature you flagged is NOT a schema mismatch — it's the rev-guard: the golden fixture tests call `TypedHomeFeedDecoder.decode(bytes)` DIRECTLY, bypassing the rev-aware `ProjectionMergeCache`; and `ProjectionCacheTest` only ever used advancing revs. The LIVE path (`KernelModel.decodeUpdate`) runs `projectionCache.merge()` FIRST, which skips a Changed row when `incomingRev <= cached.rev`. The app-owned home key emitted `projection_rev=0` every tick (the NMP bug I already fixed in #2952), so the cache committed the first empty frame and skipped every later card frame → "decodedRev advances but 0 cards." Note the host `ProjectionCache.kt`/`.swift` are BOTH generated ("DO NOT EDIT BY HAND", from NMP codegen) — so there's no hand-editable host mismatch anyway, and they're correct given a contract-compliant rev. \n  \n So the fix is NMP #2952 (emit content-advancing projection_rev for app-owned keys) — one wire-contract fix, iOS+Android+web corrected at once, no host-decode change. I did NOT fabricate a Chirp schema fix for a non-bug.
